WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.067
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.467
Here at "The Tonight Show,"
we love songs.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:05.367
And we especially love songs
written by

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:07.467
our great audience members
in under an hour.

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:10.501
It's time for "Battle of the
Instant Songwriters."

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:14.234
-♪ Sing a song
and I'm singing a song ♪

00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:19.634
♪ And I'm writing a song
about another song ♪

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:22.200
-Welcome to "Battle of the
Instant Songwriters."

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.167
Before the show, we went through
our audience and picked out

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:26.067
two people who said that they
were musicians.

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:28.000
We gave them each
a made-up song title

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.033
then gave them an hour to write
an original song

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:31.367
based on that title.

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:34.133
Here's a shot of them practicing
backstage a minute ago.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:36.200
Let's see what they came up
with and meet them right now.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.334
Come on over, guys.

00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:39.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:42.567
Hi. Nice to meet you.
-Nice to meet you.

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:44.033
-Thanks for being here.
Welcome.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.200
Welcome to the show. Let's start
with contestant number one.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.567
What is your name
and where are you from?

00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:51.934
-My name is Zaniah, and I'm
from Louisville, Kentucky.

00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:56.067
-Hey, Zaniah, welcome.
-Thank you.

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:58.534
-What was the title of the song
you were given?

00:00:58.534 --> 00:01:01.601
-"Stuck on a Ski Lift
with Jennifer Coolidge."

00:01:01.601 --> 00:01:03.601
-Oh. Fantastic.

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:05.400
And what instrument will you
be playing for this?

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.801
-The guitar.
-The guitar. Go get set up.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.200
Thank you very much
for being here.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.067
I appreciate it.
Get ready. Get to the stage.

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:15.834
Get in the zone. I love this.
Alright.

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:19.667
Right now, ladies and gentlemen,
here to perform

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:22.801
the world premiere of
the soon-to-be classic

00:01:22.801 --> 00:01:26.968
"Stuck on a Ski Lift with
Jennifer Coolidge," it's Zaniah.

00:01:26.968 --> 00:01:31.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:37.934
-♪ Who would have known I'd be
in Utah, Salt Lake City ♪

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:43.501
♪ It's winter break and finally
tryin' something exciting ♪

00:01:43.501 --> 00:01:49.234
♪ Well, so I thought it was,
went skiing for some fun ♪

00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:54.234
♪ Next thing you know I'm stuck
30 feet up above ♪

00:01:54.234 --> 00:01:59.934
♪ Now I'm stuck on a ski lift
with Jennifer Coolidge ♪

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:05.701
♪ She's so iconic,
I hope I don't sound foolish ♪

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:08.501
♪ Should I tell her
I love her? ♪

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:11.334
♪ Maybe that's way too forward ♪

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:14.167
♪ I should just keep it simple ♪

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.901
♪ Tell her I love
"White Lotus" ♪

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:23.868
♪ I'm stuck on a ski lift with
Jennifer Coolidge ♪

00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:26.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:28.334
Thank you.
-Wow!

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:30.934
Fantastic! Zaniah!

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:33.067
I don't know how, but you made
that sound cool.

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:35.601
That was amazing. Alright, let's
meet contestant number two.

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:36.801
What is your name
and where are you from?

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:39.000
-My name is Darryl Rahn.
I'm from Utica, New York.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.634
-Hey, Darryl. Utica?
Oh, my gosh, I love Utica.

00:02:42.634 --> 00:02:46.234
Darryl, tell everyone
what your song title is.

00:02:46.234 --> 00:02:49.534
-It's "2023
(Go to the Gym for Me)."

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:51.501
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:53.234
-And what instrument will you be
playing tonight?

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:54.534
-Guitar.
-Hey, there you go.

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:55.968
Double guitar tonight.
Fantastic.

00:02:55.968 --> 00:02:57.133
Go on the stage and get ready,
Darryl.

00:02:57.133 --> 00:02:59.133
Thank you for being here.

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:02.567
Get in the zone.
Get that inspiration.

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.868
You got to feel this one.

00:03:04.868 --> 00:03:06.801
2023, here we go. I like this.

00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:09.300
Ladies and gentlemen, get ready
for the world premiere of

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:13.234
"2023 (Go to the Gym for Me)"
by Darryl Rahn.

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:15.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:17.667
♪♪

00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:20.767
-♪ Woke up New Year's Day ♪

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:23.467
♪ Looked down at my phone ♪

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:26.033
♪ At all the pretty people ♪

00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:29.167
♪ Getting ripped
and getting toned ♪

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:32.367
♪ I was filled
with inspiration ♪

00:03:32.367 --> 00:03:35.501
♪ Then I turned on my TV ♪

00:03:37.167 --> 00:03:39.968
♪ It's 2023 ♪

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:42.601
♪ Go to the gym for me ♪

00:03:42.601 --> 00:03:44.434
[ Cheers ]

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:50.334
♪ The membership's expensive,
plus it's way too far to walk ♪

00:03:50.334 --> 00:03:55.400
♪ And picking up my clothes
technically counts as a squat ♪

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:56.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.868 --> 00:04:02.434
♪ But I think it's amazing
that you're doing pilates ♪

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:06.734
♪ It's 2023 ♪

00:04:06.734 --> 00:04:09.200
♪ Go to the gym for me ♪

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:10.968 --> 00:04:14.400
♪ Why would I get on
a treadmill ♪

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.000
♪ When I could simply
sit still ♪

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:21.067
♪ Just breathing in the steam of
mac and cheese ♪

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:23.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:29.167
♪ Maybe I will do a crunch
in '24 ♪

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:32.133
♪ But it's 2023 ♪

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:35.367
♪ So go to the gym for me ♪

00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:37.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:37.801 --> 00:04:40.701
-Yo! Come on now. Give it up
for Darryl, everybody.

00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:42.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
Darryl Rahn.

00:04:42.734 --> 00:04:45.868
Both of you guys, fantastic.
Now it is time to see who won.

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:48.334
We're going to let our audience
decide the winner.

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:49.968
Yeah. Aren't you lucky?

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:51.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.033 --> 00:04:51.868
[ Drumroll ]

00:04:51.868 --> 00:04:54.000
Was it Zaniah?

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:56.334 --> 00:04:58.367
Or was it Darryl?

00:04:58.367 --> 00:04:59.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:00.934
It looks like we have a winner.

00:05:00.934 --> 00:05:03.534
It is Darryl Rahn.
Congratulations, Darryl.

00:05:04.734 --> 00:05:09.200
Darryl, you are going home with
an "I love music" sweatshirt.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.467
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

00:05:10.467 --> 00:05:12.234
Also you're going to get
a notebook here

00:05:12.234 --> 00:05:14.534
so you can write more songs,
a "Tonight Show" notebook.

00:05:14.534 --> 00:05:18.000
-Thank you.
-And also $1,000 in there.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.167
That's it, come on.

00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:21.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:23.033 --> 00:05:25.701
Zaniah, no one goes home
empty-handed here.

00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:27.767
You also go home with
a sweatshirt...

00:05:27.767 --> 00:05:30.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
...that says "I love music."

00:05:30.434 --> 00:05:32.234
-Thank you.

00:05:32.234 --> 00:05:34.968
-And you also get a notebook
and $1,000!

00:05:34.968 --> 00:05:36.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's what I'm talking about.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.100
Keep writing! Keep performing!

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.501
Come back and be on the show
one day again.

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:42.701
Give it up for your two new
instant songwriters.

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:46.300
Stick around. We'll be right
back with Winston Duke. Come on!

